{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>On the first [day]</b> — defective vav. Until six hours, permitted to retain leaven:" "<b>In the evening you shall eat unleavened bread</b> — defective vav. Six days, optional to eat matzah:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The word בראשין (Exodus 12:18) is spelled defectively without a vav; the gematria of the missing vav (=6) is read as 'six hours' of the day.", 1 "The word מצת (Exodus 12:18) is spelled defectively without a vav; the missing vav (=6) is read as 'six days' during which eating matzah is optional (רשות), i.e., permitted but not obligatory outside the first night."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:37.450732678Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}